# Guiding Center 4d (Tokamak): 2nd Poincaré Integral Invariant with Gauss-Legendre VPRK Methods and Projections

The second Poincaré integral invariant

```math
I_{2} = \int_{S} \omega_{ij} (q) \, dq^{i} \wedge dq^{j}
```

of the four-dimensional guiding centre dynamics, on the same surface as the
[Gauss-Legendre Runge-Kutta page](guiding-center-4d-poincare-2nd-tokamak-firk-gauss.md): a ``0.1
\times 0.1`` square in the poloidal plane of the medium-size axisymmetric tokamak about ``(R, Z) =
(1.75, 0)``, at ``u = 0.5`` and ``\mu = 10^{-3}``.

Here the dynamics is integrated in its variational formulation, with the Gauss-Legendre variational
partitioned Runge-Kutta methods and each of the projections onto the constraint submanifold —
comparing the methods that preserve the structure of the dynamics with those that do not is the
point of these pages. The internal stage projection has no integrator in
GeometricIntegrators 0.16 and its runs fail here, as they do on the trajectory pages.

Each method is run over the same time interval at four time steps, ``\Delta t \in \{10, 5, 2, 1\}``,
whose relative errors are drawn as four curves in one figure, as on the
[Gauss-Legendre Runge-Kutta page](guiding-center-4d-poincare-2nd-tokamak-firk-gauss.md). The
projection is what separates the runs, by orders of magnitude at every one of the four time steps.

```julia
run_poincare(:tokamak, iodeproblem, "Guiding Center 4d Tokamak", tableaus_vprk_gauss())
```
